@page "/derived"
@inject CharacterSession Session

<PageTitle>Derived stats — Prowlers &amp; Paragons</PageTitle>

<h1>Derived stats</h1>
<p class="muted">
    Nothing on this page is bought. All three are computed from what is already on the
    sheet, by <code>DerivedStatsCalculator</code> — the same code the terminal wizard and
    the tests run.
</p>

<section class="panel">
    <div class="stat-blocks">
        <div class="stat-block">
            <div class="label">Edge</div>
            <div class="value">@Session.Derived.CalculateEdge(Session.Sheet)</div>
        </div>
        <div class="stat-block">
            <div class="label">Health</div>
            <div class="value">@Session.Derived.CalculateHealth(Session.Sheet)</div>
        </div>
        <div class="stat-block">
            <div class="label">Resolve</div>
            <div class="value">@Session.Derived.CalculateResolve(Session.Sheet)</div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="panel">
    <div class="panel-head"><h2>Where they come from</h2></div>

    <h3>Edge</h3>
    <p class="small">
        Perception + the better of Agility and Intellect. Three details are easy to get
        wrong and were all bugs at one point: <b>Danger Sense replaces</b> Perception rather
        than adding to it, <b>Lightning Reflexes is a flat +6</b> with no rank, and
        <b>Super Speed</b> floors Edge at its rank × 3.
    </p>
    <ul class="small muted">
        <li>Perception @Session.Sheet.GetAbilityRank("perception")d, Agility @Session.Sheet.GetAbilityRank("agility")d, Intellect @Session.Sheet.GetAbilityRank("intellect")d</li>
        @if (Session.Sheet.HasPower("danger_sense"))
        {
            <li>Danger Sense is on the sheet, so it stands in for Perception.</li>
        }
        @if (Session.Sheet.HasPower("lightning_reflexes"))
        {
            <li>Lightning Reflexes adds a flat +@DerivedStatsCalculator.LightningReflexesEdgeBonus.</li>
        }
        @if (Session.Sheet.HasPower("super_speed"))
        {
            <li>Super Speed sets a floor of its rank × 3.</li>
        }
    </ul>

    <h3>Health</h3>
    <p class="small">
        The better of (Toughness + Might) and (Toughness + Willpower), halved and rounded
        up. Halves always round up — the rulebook has a global rule for it in Ch.1.
    </p>
    <p class="small muted">
        Toughness @Session.Sheet.GetAbilityRank("toughness")d,
        Might @Session.Sheet.GetAbilityRank("might")d,
        Willpower @Session.Sheet.GetAbilityRank("willpower")d
    </p>

    <h3>Resolve</h3>
    <p class="small">
        Twice the gap between the Trait Cap and your highest relevant rank, plus one for
        each point of Determination bought (@DerivedStatsCalculator.DeterminationHpPerResolve HP
        apiece), plus one for every Condition and Plot Hook flaw. A specialist with a rank
        at the cap starts on nothing; a generalist starts with room to spend.
    </p>
    <p class="small muted">
        Trait Cap @(Session.TraitCap)d ·
        @Session.Sheet.Flaws.Count(IsResolveFlaw) Condition/Plot Hook flaw(s)
    </p>
</section>

<StepButtons Back="gear" BackLabel="Gear" Next="finishing" NextLabel="Finishing touches" />

@code {
    private bool IsResolveFlaw(SelectedFlaw sf) =>
        Session.Rules.GetFlaw(sf.FlawId)?.FlawType is "condition" or "plot_hook" or "plot_hook_and_condition";
}
